The corrections src/V2/Raw needs on top of what the generator emits. The
regeneration job, .github/workflows/regenerate-client.yml, re-applies them
after every generation and fails when they no longer apply.

1. The generator encodes request bodies with \GuzzleHttp\Utils::jsonEncode(),
   a method Guzzle 7 introduced. The package supports Guzzle 6 as well, whose
   GuzzleHttp\Utils has no such method, so every call site goes through
   ObjectSerializer::guzzleJsonEncode(), which hands the data to whichever
   encoder the installed Guzzle provides.

2. The generator passes ObjectSerializer::deserialize() model names without a
   namespace, which resolve against the global namespace and are not found.
   The deserializer prefixes the model namespace when the name it was handed
   is not a class of its own.
   See https://github.com/OpenAPITools/openapi-generator/issues/3136

Both corrections are mechanical. To refresh this patch after a generation
moved the lines it touches, apply the two corrections to the raw generation
and diff that against the generation.

